From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: a733: say in the DT that SMHC2 is a soldered eMMC

`mmc@4022000` has carried `non-removable` since `arm64-dts-allwinner-a733-add-sd-emmc`, and nothing else. So the
node describes a controller that merely happens to keep its card, and the core
treats it as one: every `mmc_rescan_try_freq()` still opens with an SDIO reset
and a full SD attach before it ever reaches `mmc_attach_mmc()`. Read the
guards in drivers/mmc/core/core.c (6.18.36):

    2119   if (!(host->caps2 & MMC_CAP2_NO_SDIO))
    2120           sdio_reset(host);
    2122   mmc_go_idle(host);
    2124   if (!(host->caps2 & MMC_CAP2_NO_SD)) {
    2125           if (mmc_send_if_cond_pcie(host, host->ocr_avail))
    2127           if (mmc_card_sd_express(host))
    2132   if (!(host->caps2 & MMC_CAP2_NO_SDIO))
    2133           if (!mmc_attach_sdio(host))
    2136   if (!(host->caps2 & MMC_CAP2_NO_SD))
    2137           if (!mmc_attach_sd(host))
    2140   if (!(host->caps2 & MMC_CAP2_NO_MMC))
    2141           if (!mmc_attach_mmc(host))

Four call sites, all gated by the two bits this patch sets. There is no card
slot on SMHC2 to find anything in: the device is soldered -- U8A, a Samsung
KLM8G1GETF-B041, schematic V1.10 p9 -- and it has no SDIO function. So the DT
gets `no-sd` and `no-sdio`, read by drivers/mmc/core/host.c:401-404.

`mmc-ddr-1_8v` is the second half of the same point. DDR52 works on this board
today, but only as a side effect: sunxi-mmc.c hands MMC_CAP_1_8V_DDR (and
MMC_CAP_3_3V_DDR) to *every* new-timings host, before mmc_of_parse() runs. That
is a statement about the controller family. What the board says is the card:
EXT_CSD[196] DEVICE_TYPE reads 0x57 on the fitted part, i.e. bits 0/1/2/4/6 =
HS26, HS52, DDR52-1.8V, HS200-1.8V, HS400-1.8V. Reader:
drivers/mmc/core/host.c:387-388.

And the same statement on the host side, drivers/mmc/host/sunxi-mmc.c:
`MMC_CAP2_NO_SD | MMC_CAP2_NO_SDIO` in sunxi_mmc_probe().

    ! This bit must NOT be set unconditionally. One and the same driver
    ! serves SMHC0, the SD slot that carries root on the 8 GiB board and the 6 GiB board, and
    ! mmc_of_parse() never clears these two bits. An ungated
    ! mmc->caps2 |= MMC_CAP2_NO_SD would make mmc_attach_sd() unreachable
    ! on SMHC0 and the SD card would never enumerate again.

It is therefore gated on a new per-cfg flag, `emmc_only`, set on
`sun60i_a733_emmc_cfg` alone -- the same shape as `can_hs400`, `can_auto_cmd23`
and `can_hsq` already in that struct. The other SoCs' `-emmc` cfgs are left
untouched: no board here can measure them.

`cap-mmc-hw-reset` is KEPT, with the card-side state written into the node.
The board side is real, and both citations were re-read for this patch rather
than taken over:

  - schematic V1.10 p7, ball 1AB23: net EMMC_RST on
    `PC1/NAND-ALE/SDC2-RST/SDC3-RST/PC-EINT1`;
  - schematic V1.10 p9, U8A pin RST: the same net at the package;
  - and `mmc2_clk_pins` in this DTS already muxes PC1 to function "mmc2".

The host can drive it: sunxi_mmc_hw_reset() toggles SMHC_HWRST and is hooked as
`.card_hw_reset`. The card ignores it: EXT_CSD[162] RST_N_FUNCTION reads 0x00
= "RST_n temporarily disabled", so mmc_card_can_reset()
(drivers/mmc/core/mmc.c:2300-2306) is false and _mmc_hw_reset() falls to its
power-cycle branch (mmc.c:2319-2328).

    ! That branch resets nothing on this board either. vmmc is SWOUT2 and
    ! vqmmc is CLDO5; both are `regulator-always-on` and both are shared
    ! with an I/O bank supply (vcc-ph / vcc-pc in the pinctrl node), so
    ! mmc_power_cycle() cannot drop the card's rails. Today this eMMC has
    ! no working reset of any kind. That is a finding, not something this
    ! patch fixes.

Dropping the property would not improve that; it would only delete the true
statement that the host can drive RST_N, and it would remove the precondition
for the one reset that could work here. Note also that
mmc_hw_reset_for_init() (core.c:2048-2055) checks MMC_CAP_HW_RESET and
`ops->card_hw_reset` but NOT mmc_card_can_reset() -- so with the property the
pin is already asserted before each init; it is the card's RST_N_FUNCTION, not
Linux, that makes it a no-op. Turning the card side on means programming
RST_N_FUNCTION = 0x1, which is permanent and irreversible. That is a separate
decision with its own evidence, not part of a wiring baseline.

`fixed-emmc-driver-type` is deliberately NOT set. The card offers five driver
types (EXT_CSD[197] DRIVER_STRENGTH = 0x1f) and we run type B because nothing
selects one: EXT_CSD[185] HS_TIMING reads 0x03 and its driver-type nibble
[7:4] is 0. Any value here would be a guess about pad and trace impedance. The
node carries a comment naming the experiment that would earn one; the reader,
if it is ever set, is drivers/mmc/core/host.c:412-414 ->
mmc_select_driver_type() (mmc.c:1356).

Card-side values: `mmc extcsd`-style raw dump taken on the 8 GiB board, 2026-09-19, from
the eMMC this image runs on. Bytes 162 / 185 / 196 / 197 = 0x00 / 0x03 / 0x57 /
0x1f.

Verified -- three separate claims:

  - applies: `patch -p1 --fuzz=0` over a freshly unpacked pristine 6.18.36
    with the full numbered series, 184 of 184, no fuzz, no reject (2026-09-19).
  - builds, DT half only: `cpp` + `dtc -I dts -O dtb` on the applied tree,
    0 warnings, and checked in the *output* rather than the source -- the
    decompiled dtb's `mmc@4022000` carries `mmc-ddr-1_8v`, `no-sd`, `no-sdio`
    and `cap-mmc-hw-reset`, and carries no `fixed-emmc-driver-type`. All four
    properties are in `mmc-controller-common.yaml`, so the node still passes
    the sunxi binding's `unevaluatedProperties: false`.
  - builds, C half: ✅ compiled by the automated build (compile-gate + full kernel).
    Not built by the author; the pipeline result is the witness.
  - silicon: NOT verified. Nothing in this patch has been on a board.

Pending, as one observable on hardware: on a boot of a kernel carrying this
patch, an MMC command trace of `4022000.mmc` over a rescan contains no CMD52
and no CMD8/ACMD41 SD sequence -- only CMD0/CMD1/CMD2/CMD3 -- while
`4020000.mmc` still enumerates the SD card normally. That single boot
falsifies both halves at once: the eMMC skipping the SD/SDIO attach, and the
gate not having leaked onto the SD controller.

Assisted-by: Claude
---

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s-minimal.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s-minimal.dts
@@ -887,9 +887,92 @@
 			max-frequency = <200000000>;
 			non-removable;
 			cap-mmc-highspeed;
+
+			/*
+			 * The card answers DDR52 at 1.8 V: EXT_CSD[196]
+			 * DEVICE_TYPE reads 0x57 on the fitted part
+			 * (the 8 GiB board, 2026-09-19), i.e. bits 0/1/2/4/6 =
+			 * HS26, HS52, DDR52-1.8V, HS200-1.8V, HS400-1.8V.
+			 * Say so here. Today the bit already arrives from the
+			 * driver, which hands MMC_CAP_1_8V_DDR to every
+			 * new-timings host (sunxi-mmc.c, the
+			 * clk_delays||use_new_timings block before
+			 * mmc_of_parse()); that is a controller default, not a
+			 * statement about this board's card.
+			 * Reader: drivers/mmc/core/host.c:387-388.
+			 */
+			mmc-ddr-1_8v;
 			mmc-hs200-1_8v;
 			mmc-hs400-1_8v;
+
+			/*
+			 * Soldered eMMC at footprint U8A. ⚠ The schematic
+			 * symbol carries KLM8G1GETF-B041 (V1.10 p9); the part
+			 * actually fitted on the 8 GiB board is a SanDisk iNAND
+			 * SDINBDV4-32G -- package photo, and sysfs reads
+			 * manfid 0x45, name DV4032, 29.1 GiB (2026-09-19).
+			 * Either way it is soldered: no removable card and no SDIO
+			 * function can ever appear on SMHC2, so every rescan
+			 * may skip the SD and SDIO halves of the probe:
+			 * sdio_reset()'s CMD52, mmc_send_if_cond_pcie(),
+			 * mmc_attach_sdio() and mmc_attach_sd()
+			 * (drivers/mmc/core/core.c:2119-2138 -- each of those
+			 * four call sites is guarded by exactly these two
+			 * caps2 bits).
+			 * Readers: drivers/mmc/core/host.c:401-404.
+			 */
+			no-sd;
+			no-sdio;
+
+			/*
+			 * RST_N is wired on the board: net EMMC_RST runs from
+			 * PC1 (PC1/NAND-ALE/SDC2-RST/SDC3-RST/PC-EINT1,
+			 * schematic V1.10 p7 ball 1AB23) to the card's RST pin
+			 * (p9, U8A pin RST), and mmc2_clk_pins above muxes PC1
+			 * to the mmc2 function. The host drives it from
+			 * SMHC_HWRST (sunxi-mmc.c sunxi_mmc_hw_reset(), hooked
+			 * as .card_hw_reset), and this property is what arms
+			 * that path (drivers/mmc/core/host.c:372-373 ->
+			 * MMC_CAP_HW_RESET).
+			 *
+			 * The card currently ignores the signal:
+			 * EXT_CSD[162] RST_N_FUNCTION reads 0x00 on the fitted
+			 * part (the 8 GiB board, 2026-09-19) = "RST_n temporarily
+			 * disabled". So mmc_card_can_reset() is false
+			 * (drivers/mmc/core/mmc.c:2300-2306) and _mmc_hw_reset()
+			 * takes its power-cycle branch
+			 * (drivers/mmc/core/mmc.c:2319-2328) -- which on this
+			 * board resets nothing either, because vmmc (SWOUT2)
+			 * and vqmmc (CLDO5) are regulator-always-on and are
+			 * shared with the PH and PC I/O banks.
+			 *
+			 * The property stays because it describes the board and
+			 * the host, which is this node's job, and because it is
+			 * the precondition for the only reset that could ever
+			 * work here. Enabling it at the card is a one-time
+			 * programming of RST_N_FUNCTION = 0x1 (permanent, not
+			 * reversible) and is therefore a separate decision with
+			 * its own evidence, not part of the wiring.
+			 */
 			cap-mmc-hw-reset;
+
+			/*
+			 * fixed-emmc-driver-type is deliberately absent.
+			 * The card offers five types: EXT_CSD[197]
+			 * DRIVER_STRENGTH = 0x1f (the 8 GiB board, 2026-09-19), and we run
+			 * type B today because nothing selects one --
+			 * EXT_CSD[185] HS_TIMING reads 0x03, whose driver-type
+			 * nibble [7:4] is 0. Picking a value without measuring
+			 * it would be a guess about pad/trace impedance.
+			 * The experiment that would settle it: sweep
+			 * fixed-emmc-driver-type 0..4 on the 8 GiB board and record, per
+			 * value, HS400 re-tune count and the CRC/end-bit error
+			 * histogram from sunxi_mmc_dump_errinfo() over a fixed
+			 * write soak. Until that exists, no value here.
+			 * Reader, when it is set: drivers/mmc/core/host.c:412-414
+			 * -> host->fixed_drv_type, consumed by
+			 * mmc_select_driver_type() (drivers/mmc/core/mmc.c:1356).
+			 */
 			#address-cells = <1>;
 			#size-cells = <0>;
 			status = "okay";
--- a/drivers/mmc/host/sunxi-mmc.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/host/sunxi-mmc.c
@@ -391,6 +391,16 @@
 	 * the host is then the only thing that waits for the card's busy.
 	 */
 	bool can_hsq;
+
+	/*
+	 * The compatible this cfg is reached by names a controller instance
+	 * that is wired to a soldered eMMC device: no removable card, no SDIO
+	 * function. Lets the core skip the SD and SDIO halves of every probe.
+	 * Must stay per-cfg: one and the same driver serves the SD slot on this
+	 * SoC, and an unconditional MMC_CAP2_NO_SD there would stop the card
+	 * that carries root from ever attaching.
+	 */
+	bool emmc_only;
 };
 
 struct sunxi_mmc_host {
@@ -2243,6 +2253,7 @@
 	.can_auto_cmd23 = true,
 	.can_wait_busy = true,
 	.can_hsq = true,
+	.emmc_only = true,
 	/* UM 11.3.8.17 recommends BSIZE_OF_TRANS = 3 (MSize 16), TX_TL = 240
 	 * and RX_TL = 15, and 11.3.6.2 writes 0x300F00F0 verbatim.
 	 * Vendor silicon on the 8 GiB board reads exactly this while writing this eMMC
@@ -2601,6 +2612,19 @@
 			goto error_free_dma;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * A controller wired to a soldered eMMC has no SD card and no SDIO
+	 * function to find, so mmc_rescan_try_freq() may go straight to
+	 * mmc_attach_mmc(): these two bits are what gate sdio_reset()'s CMD52,
+	 * mmc_send_if_cond_pcie(), mmc_attach_sdio() and mmc_attach_sd()
+	 * (mmc/core/core.c). The board says the same thing through no-sd /
+	 * no-sdio in the DT and the two agree: mmc_of_parse() below only ORs
+	 * these two bits in (core/host.c:401-404), and its single caps2 clear
+	 * is "no-mmc-hs400", which touches the HS400 bits alone.
+	 */
+	if (host->cfg->emmc_only)
+		mmc->caps2 |= MMC_CAP2_NO_SD | MMC_CAP2_NO_SDIO;
+
 	ret = mmc_of_parse(mmc);
 	if (ret)
 		goto error_free_dma;
